  "body": "From the review of PR #147 (#112, https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/147#issuecomment-6713447728):\n\n1. The 'machine states no <kind> coolant code' refusal doesn't name the operation. With several ops, the user can't tell which one asked for it.\n2. Machine coolant names must match exactly (`mist`, `through-spindle`, `through-tool`), but the machine editor takes free text, so 'Through spindle' is refused with a confusing message. The editor should offer the known kinds, or the docs should list them.\n3. A machine with no Flood code still posts a Flood op with no coolant code and no warning: it cuts dry without telling anyone. A Flood op on a machine without a flood code should warn by name, or block like the other kinds.\n4. A user post that doesn't read `PARAM Coolant` posts Off/Mist ops as Flood silently. Consider a post-capability flag so such a post refuses non-Flood ops.\n\nAlso owed tests: coolant through the Fanuc Lathe post; M88 on the shipped mill-turn machine; the UI dropdown path; a Mist→Flood sequence.",
